# Accepted gitleaks findings, one fingerprint per line.
#
# A fingerprint is commit:path:rule:line, so an entry stops applying the
# moment the finding moves. That is deliberate — a blanket path or rule
# exclusion would keep hiding a real secret introduced later in the same file.
#
# f3c4d0c5 — internal/mcp/resources_test.go, `private-key` rule.
# The fixture is a table of deliberately fake credential files
# (".env", "deploy.pem", "id_ed25519", …) used to prove that the MCP file
# resource refuses to serve them. The matched value is the literal string
# "-----BEGIN OPENSSH PRIVATE KEY-----" with no key material after it. The
# test has since moved to internal/mcp/protocol_test.go; this entry covers
# only the historical commit, which cannot be edited without a rewrite.
f3c4d0c5e212a57480c3e3ba3b5c1af46f20b23a:internal/mcp/resources_test.go:private-key:479

# 26e13d17 — internal/mcp/eval_test.go, `stripe-access-token` rule.
# The eval suite's fixture workspace contains a ".env" whose value must be
# recognisable as a credential, because the scenarios assert it is never the
# answer to a symbol lookup or a content search. The value written had a
# live-Stripe-key prefix followed by an ordinary identifier: no key material,
# and no account it could belong to, but enough shape for the scanner.
#
# The value is deliberately not repeated here. A first attempt at this comment
# quoted it, and the explanation tripped the same rule in the very file that
# exists to record the exception.
#
# The fixture now reads "fixture-not-a-real-key-…", so this cannot recur. This
# entry covers only the historical commit, which cannot be edited without a
# rewrite.
26e13d17a94449f664ca03d43003961e5891e480:internal/mcp/eval_test.go:stripe-access-token:89

# ec0cb037 — .gitleaksignore itself, `stripe-access-token` rule.
# The entry above originally quoted the fixture value it was explaining, so
# the comment recording the exception became a finding in its own right. The
# text has been rewritten to describe the value instead of repeating it; this
# entry covers the one commit where it was quoted.
#
# The lesson, recorded because it is not obvious: a file that documents
# credential-shaped findings must describe them, never quote them.
ec0cb0374690ae5eb79efa1f34fa018bbffb84d9:.gitleaksignore:stripe-access-token:20
